1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,000
SplitShield — detect, repair, and quantify hidden leakage in computer-vision datasets.

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:12,500
Duplicates that cross the train/test boundary quietly inflate reported accuracy.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Let's audit a real dataset on the live app — a ZIP of game-sprite images.

4
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:26,000
Uploads are validated by file signature and safely extracted — nothing is ever executed.

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:30,800
One click: Start audit.

6
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:39,000
The pipeline runs for real: indexing, SHA-256 exact matching, perceptual hashing…

7
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:50,500
…then appearance-embedding similarity search, scoring, and report generation.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Integrity Score 65.9 — high risk. 399 near-duplicate cross-split leaks detected.

9
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:06,500
Every chart is computed from this audit: split sizes, classes, and severities.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Evidence Explorer: each suspicious pair, side by side, with its similarity evidence.

11
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:21,000
A human makes the call — confirm leakage, mark safe or expected, or flag uncertain.

12
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:27,500
Review decisions are recorded without overwriting the algorithmic evidence.

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:35,500
Repair Studio proposes a safer split — 61 duplicate groups, every move explained.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Originals are never modified; the repair manifest exports as CSV or JSON.

15
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,500
The audit report: score breakdown, findings with review status, and full configuration.

16
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:58,500
Dataset fingerprint, random seed, and package versions — anyone can re-run and verify.

17
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Everything downloads as a printable report, JSON, or CSV.

18
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:11,500
The methodology is public: SHA-256, perceptual hashing, embeddings, and the score formula.

19
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,200
A fully documented REST API underneath.

20
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:21,800
Recent audits stay on your own device — privacy by design, auto-deleted on the server.

21
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:28,500
SplitShield — audit your splits before you trust your accuracy.
